# Rendered media and machine-local state. The studio's SOURCE is text: .movie files,
# preset JSON, variables.json, cards, scripts. Anything a render produces can be
# regenerated from those and does not belong in history.

# ---- renders and intermediates ----
_work/
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.webm
*.wav
*.mp3
*.srt

# ---- model weights, never ----
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.onnx

# ---- logs and scratch ----
*.log
# nohup render logs land as .out beside the .log ones and are the same thing
*.out
studio/samples/_scratch/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- full-size stills live in ComfyUI's output, not here ----
# The 640x360 card panels ARE kept: they are the evidence for what each variable
# does, and at WebP q82 the whole set is ~31 MB. Their 1.3 GB originals stay in
# ~/ComfyUI/output/claude-generated/studio_cards/.
*.png
!studio/samples/**/*.png

# The generation corpus. The MANIFEST is tracked - it is the reproducible recipe for
# every image and the thing worth reviewing in a diff - but the images themselves are
# regenerable from it and would grow without bound.
studio/samples/gallery/

# The cast proof run, same policy applied to the same kind of thing. 146 individual arm
# cells at full size are 194 MB and are regenerable from studio/_tools/cast_proof.py; the
# CONTACT SHEETS sitting beside them are 11 MB of jpg, are what a person actually reads,
# and stay tracked - as do _metrics.json and _card_patches.json, which are the findings.
studio/samples/cast_proof/*/

# A mirror of the reference sheets, which live in ComfyUI/input and are not served from
# there. serve.py:_mirror_sheet re-copies any missing file on the next request, so this is
# a cache, not a source, and it duplicates bytes that already exist on the box.
studio/samples/_refsheets/

# The character sweeps. SAME POLICY AS gallery/ AND cast_proof/ ABOVE, applied to the
# thing that has grown fastest: one reference character now has ~600 renders behind her
# and every future cast member inherits the same template. What a person reads is the
# CONTACT SHEET, the measurements.json and the verdicts.json, and those stay tracked -
# they are the evidence a claim rests on and the thing worth reviewing in a diff. The
# individual full-size cells behind them are regenerable by re-running the tool that made
# them, which is named in each sweep's docstring, and 600 MB of PNG per character would
# put this repository past what a git host will take.
# KEPT ON PURPOSE, against this rule: samples/cast/<ID>/ (the turnaround IS the training
# set and the reference asset), terra_styles/cells/ (250 small webp, and the dossier page
# renders every one of them), terra_motion/strips|faces (the frame strips ARE the evidence
# for every motion verdict, since nothing was watched as video).
studio/samples/cast/*_views/yaw/
studio/samples/cast/*_views/yaw_rotate_failed/
studio/samples/cast/*_views/yawprobe/
studio/samples/cast/*_views/elevation/
studio/samples/cast/*_views/frames/
studio/samples/cast/*_views/emotions/
studio/samples/cast/*_views/_embed/
studio/samples/cast/*_motion/_frames/
studio/samples/cast/*_motion/keyframes/
studio/samples/motion_staging/detail/
studio/samples/motion_staging/strips/
studio/samples/motion_staging/percard/
studio/samples/motion_staging/grids/
studio/samples/motion_staging/keyframes/

# The prompt-replication corpus. SAME POLICY AS gallery/, cast_proof/ AND the character
# sweeps above. 111 full-size cells are 238 MB and this repository's .git is already 2.0
# GB. What a person reads is the 19 CONTACT SHEETS in _sheets/ and the 29 side-by-side
# A/B JPEGs in _compare/ - those stay tracked, as do _measured.json, the analysis, and the
# per-cell recipe sidecar beside every image, which is the reproducible recipe and the
# thing worth reviewing in a diff. The cells are regenerable by
# `studio/_tools/replicate_prompts.py` and they remain on disk here and in
# ~/ComfyUI/output/claude-generated/replicated/ - they are simply not carried in history.
# _look/ is a downscaled cache of those same cells, so it goes with them.
# NOTE, recorded rather than quietly fixed: studio/samples/flux2/ committed its 58
# full-size cells (107 MB) in 1a8feac before this rule was written. That is not undone
# here - rewriting history to save 107 MB is a worse trade than the inconsistency.
studio/samples/replicated/base/*.png
studio/samples/replicated/extra/*.png
studio/samples/replicated/zimage/*.png
studio/samples/replicated/_look/

# The FLUX.2 physical-media gallery. SAME POLICY AS gallery/, cast_proof/, the character
# sweeps and replicated/ above, applied to the largest corpus yet: 418 full-size cells at
# 1536px are 1.2 GB, and .git is already 2.0 GB. Every .png in here has a sibling .json
# carrying its complete recipe - engine, checkpoint, text encoder, VAE, workflow, full
# prompt, seed, steps, guidance, sampler, scheduler, size, LoRA - so the corpus is
# reproducible from what stays tracked by re-running studio/_tools/flux2_gallery.py.
# KEPT ON PURPOSE: the 41 contact sheets in _sheets/ (40 MB of jpg, and the thing a person
# actually reads), index.html, _ledger.json, _dropped.json, and every per-cell recipe
# sidecar - the sidecars are the diff worth reviewing. The cells remain on disk here and
# in ~/ComfyUI/output/claude-generated/; they are simply not carried in history.
# This includes _ab/ (three-engine comparisons), _calibrate/ (Turbo on/off pairs),
# _dropped/ (the rejected frames), hex/ and typography/ - their FINDINGS live in the
# sidecars, the ledger and the contact sheets, all of which stay.
studio/samples/flux2_gallery/**/*.png

# THE COAT's render intermediates. The delivered film, the master stem and every clip are
# already covered by the *.mp4 / *.wav rules at the top of this file. What stays tracked is
# the text and the evidence a person reads: the compiled film JSON, the scripts that made
# it, CUT_REPORT.txt, mix_report.json, measurements.json, and the contact sheets, watch
# sheets, frame strips and poster as jpg. Nothing below is a finding.
studio/samples/the_film/__pycache__/
studio/samples/the_film/*.log
